  "narrationText": "GPS does not send a full calendar date. Older signals stored that week number in ten bits. The range ends at 1,023. At the limit, there is no new number left. Zero is sent again when the next week begins. Old software read zero as the previous cycle. Their displayed date jumped backward. Real time kept moving forward. An update selected the correct GPS cycle. Now the receiver shows the correct date. The number repeated. Time did not.",
